# Safety net for a build whose context is the repository ROOT (the real contexts are backend/ and frontend/, each with
# its own .dockerignore): even then nothing secret, host-specific or bulky is sent.
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
*.dump
*.sql.gz
